Subject: Install libvmdk Python bindings to Debian dist-packages without relying on distutils
Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Description: Install the libvmdk Python bindings (pyvmdk) to /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages, the destination Debian ships and python3-libvmdk.install expects, because the configure pyexecdir check falls back to /usr in this builder.
Base-Tree: debian libvmdk 20240510-1
Verify: cmd `dpkg-deb -c python3-libvmdk_20240510-1+deb13u0+dhi0_amd64.deb | grep -E '\./usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pyvmdk\.cpython-313-x86_64-linux-gnu\.so$'` expect "dist-packages/pyvmdk.cpython-313-x86_64-linux-gnu.so"
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI build environment workaround only)
Drop-When: never: the hermetic builder's python3 cannot import distutils even with setuptools installed, so AX_PYTHON falls back to /usr for pyexecdir and no Debian version bump removes the need for this path.
---
--- a/pyvmdk/Makefile.am
+++ b/pyvmdk/Makefile.am
@@ -15 +15,2 @@
-pyexec_LTLIBRARIES = pyvmdk.la
+pyvmdkdir = $(prefix)/lib/python3/dist-packages
+pyvmdk_LTLIBRARIES = pyvmdk.la
